# Runtime data. Both are mounted into the running container by
# docker-compose (uploads from the host, storage as a named volume), so a
# copy baked into the image is invisible at runtime. Including them only made
# every image carry every client's files and invoices, and every deploy
# slower as they accumulated — the build context had reached 2.75GB.
# The image creates an empty, correctly-owned /app/storage itself.
public/uploads
storage

# Logs anywhere in the tree. The top-level `*.log` above only matches the
# context root, so nginx's docker/nginx/logs/*.log slipped through.
**/*.log

# Database dumps and local tool state must never enter an image.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
.auto-claude
